Package: mysterymaps
Title: Geographic Mapping Tools for Healthcare Access Studies
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("Tyler", "Muffly", email = "tyler.muffly@dhha.org", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2044-1693"))
Description: Builds the maps healthcare access and mystery-caller studies keep
    needing: county choropleths of provider supply, dissolved drive-time coverage
    surfaces layered as mutually exclusive alternatives, provider dot maps that
    stay clickable, and the legend, label and notes furniture those require. A
    single template assembles the common case; the pieces are exported for maps
    that are not the common case. Also covers isochrone generation via the HERE
    Routing API, block-group overlap, Hospital Referral Region and ACOG district
    overlays, and state choropleths. Defaults encode decisions that are easy to
    get wrong: zero is its own colour class rather than the bottom of a gradient,
    legends follow the active base layer, and saved widgets stay self-contained.
    Companion to the 'mysterycall' mystery-caller study framework.
